# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# Evaluated before the catch-all that serves index.html for unknown paths, so
# these win as long as no real file sits at the same path.
#
# /go — the URL paid campaigns point at. Meta rejects apps.apple.com links
# under the Traffic objective, so ads need a normal web URL on our own domain
# that hops straight to the listing. 302, not 301: the ?ct= campaign token
# changes per campaign and a permanent redirect would be cached by browsers
# and CDNs long after we changed it.
#
# ?ct= is the App Store Connect campaign token — it surfaces the source under
# App Analytics -> Sources -> Campaigns. Max 50 chars, no spaces.

# Both spellings: Pages matches these as distinct paths, and /go/ without a
# rule falls through to the index.html catch-all — i.e. it quietly serves the
# whole marketing page at 200 instead of redirecting, losing the install and
# the attribution. Keep the two lines in sync.

/go   https://apps.apple.com/us/app/bailamos-latin-dance-events/id6767940322?ct=meta-citypicker  302
/go/  https://apps.apple.com/us/app/bailamos-latin-dance-events/id6767940322?ct=meta-citypicker  302
